1
00:00:01,094 --> 00:00:02,124
(Episode 25)

2
00:00:02,194 --> 00:00:03,194
Just a moment.

3
00:00:17,714 --> 00:00:18,714
Here.

4
00:00:19,674 --> 00:00:22,344
I found Ko Eun Seol's presentation file.

5
00:00:31,624 --> 00:00:33,024
How did he find it?

6
00:00:39,964 --> 00:00:42,104
If you oppose a re-evaluation here,

7
00:00:42,434 --> 00:00:44,434
they'll agree with you to your face,

8
00:00:45,334 --> 00:00:46,403
but behind your back,

9
00:00:46,404 --> 00:00:48,974
they'll call it an abuse of power by the owner's family.

10
00:00:53,984 --> 00:00:55,844
Ko Eun Seol's opponent is our daughter.

11
00:00:56,484 --> 00:00:58,354
All the more reason to give her a fair chance.

12
00:01:03,324 --> 00:01:06,024
A proper gait isn't simply about walking well.

13
00:01:06,294 --> 00:01:08,293
It's the beginning of full-body balance,

14
00:01:08,294 --> 00:01:09,364
starting from the feet.

15
00:01:11,664 --> 00:01:13,964
By efficiently distributing weight and impact,

16
00:01:14,234 --> 00:01:17,274
it reduces the burden on your knees and body...

17
00:01:17,374 --> 00:01:19,874
and helps you maintain your body's balance.

18
00:01:22,744 --> 00:01:25,674
So for the outsole that promotes a proper gait,

19
00:01:25,914 --> 00:01:27,784
I added a breathable material...

20
00:01:28,314 --> 00:01:31,114
to design walking shoes that can be worn every day.

21
00:01:36,894 --> 00:01:40,194
Now, I'll announce the results of the judges' vote.

22
00:01:40,764 --> 00:01:42,864
The winning design for the Shoejoy signature line is...

23
00:01:45,794 --> 00:01:48,304
Ko Eun Seol's design.

24
00:01:50,674 --> 00:01:51,674
Thank you.

25
00:01:52,374 --> 00:01:53,374
Thank you.

26
00:01:53,704 --> 00:01:54,704
Thank you.

27
00:02:01,114 --> 00:02:04,214
(Signature Line Design Competition)

28
00:02:11,694 --> 00:02:13,094
That was even better than I expected.

29
00:02:13,564 --> 00:02:14,994
- Thank you. - Congratulations.

30
00:02:15,064 --> 00:02:16,364
- Congratulations. - Thank you.

31
00:02:21,064 --> 00:02:22,964
- Eun Seol. - Ma'am.

32
00:02:23,404 --> 00:02:24,404
Congratulations.

33
00:02:25,104 --> 00:02:26,104
Thank you.

34
00:02:27,204 --> 00:02:29,674
I heard there was an incident this morning,

35
00:02:30,114 --> 00:02:32,674
but I'm glad the results were good.

36
00:02:33,074 --> 00:02:34,883
Thanks to your help, ma'am,

37
00:02:34,884 --> 00:02:36,914
I was able to finish my presentation.

38
00:02:38,254 --> 00:02:41,154
No matter the situation, you don't give up.

39
00:02:41,184 --> 00:02:42,924
I find that inspiring.

40
00:02:44,094 --> 00:02:48,494
The presentation with the easel was also moving.

41
00:02:49,824 --> 00:02:52,034
I'll be looking forward to what you do next.

42
00:02:52,294 --> 00:02:54,134
Yes, thank you.

43
00:03:11,014 --> 00:03:12,314
Attorney Seo.

44
00:03:13,224 --> 00:03:14,224
Congratulations.

45
00:03:15,124 --> 00:03:17,154
Wait, when did you prepare this?

46
00:03:17,624 --> 00:03:19,594
I knew you were going to win.

47
00:03:21,824 --> 00:03:23,664
But did something happen?

48
00:03:24,234 --> 00:03:25,994
You didn't answer my calls yesterday.

49
00:03:26,964 --> 00:03:29,064
How did you lose your presentation file?

50
00:03:30,774 --> 00:03:32,634
A lot of things happened.

51
00:03:32,974 --> 00:03:35,244
I'm just glad it all turned out well.

52
00:03:35,504 --> 00:03:37,113
You can tell me all about it later.

53
00:03:37,114 --> 00:03:39,374
Anyway, you did great today.

54
00:03:40,044 --> 00:03:41,784
Thank you, Attorney Seo.

55
00:03:44,354 --> 00:03:46,184
Please excuse me for a moment.

56
00:03:49,324 --> 00:03:50,394
Chief.

57
00:03:53,054 --> 00:03:54,064
Hey.

58
00:03:54,864 --> 00:03:57,394
Thank you so much for earlier.

59
00:03:57,894 --> 00:03:59,064
If it weren't for you,

60
00:03:59,134 --> 00:04:01,364
I wouldn't have been able to finish my presentation.

61
00:04:01,434 --> 00:04:02,704
I got lucky.

62
00:04:03,274 --> 00:04:04,734
The keyring caught my eye.

63
00:04:04,834 --> 00:04:08,574
I think the keyring from your mother really brought me good luck.

64
00:04:11,244 --> 00:04:12,674
That could be the case.

65
00:04:13,984 --> 00:04:16,684
I just did what I had to as the person in charge,

66
00:04:17,284 --> 00:04:19,184
so you don't have to be so grateful.

67
00:04:21,054 --> 00:04:22,054
Sure.

68
00:04:23,624 --> 00:04:25,754
Anyway, congratulations.

69
00:04:44,314 --> 00:04:45,314
Mom.

70
00:04:46,374 --> 00:04:47,944
I did well, right?

71
00:04:49,484 --> 00:04:51,154
I'm not struggling at all.

72
00:04:52,614 --> 00:04:55,154
Once again, I pushed through bravely today.

73
00:05:00,094 --> 00:05:01,094
To be honest...

74
00:05:03,564 --> 00:05:05,234
I was a little scared.

75
00:05:08,734 --> 00:05:10,104
But don't worry.

76
00:05:12,134 --> 00:05:14,604
I'm going to keep doing well, just like I did today.

77
00:05:17,444 --> 00:05:18,874
I'm your daughter, after all.

78
00:05:23,914 --> 00:05:24,914
Mom.

79
00:05:27,324 --> 00:05:28,924
Please watch over me.

80
00:05:38,034 --> 00:05:39,034
What are you doing, Eun Seol?

81
00:05:40,704 --> 00:05:42,764
I just had something to think about.

82
00:05:45,604 --> 00:05:47,504
It's been a long day, hasn't it?

83
00:05:48,304 --> 00:05:51,074
Yes, it feels like it flew by in an instant.

84
00:05:53,484 --> 00:05:57,614
You know, Eun Seol, it's incredible to watch you grow every day,

85
00:05:58,354 --> 00:06:00,354
and it makes me so proud.

86
00:06:01,884 --> 00:06:05,094
That's why I want to keep cheering you on.

87
00:06:06,254 --> 00:06:08,124
I can sense that from you,

88
00:06:08,394 --> 00:06:09,724
which makes me feel even more grateful.

89
00:06:14,064 --> 00:06:15,064
Eun Seol,

90
00:06:15,364 --> 00:06:17,834
how about we have our own little celebration tomorrow?

91
00:06:18,704 --> 00:06:21,844
- What? - Let's have dinner tomorrow.

92
00:06:24,214 --> 00:06:25,214
I'd like that.

93
00:06:35,784 --> 00:06:38,854
What time is it? Why isn't she home yet?

94
00:06:39,754 --> 00:06:40,764
Director Joo,

95
00:06:41,024 --> 00:06:42,724
is Hae Ra still not answering her phone?

96
00:06:43,224 --> 00:06:44,964
I'm afraid not.

97
00:06:45,364 --> 00:06:47,333
That means we haven't been able to reach her...

98
00:06:47,334 --> 00:06:49,004
since she stormed out earlier.

99
00:06:50,104 --> 00:06:51,104
That's right.

100
00:06:51,734 --> 00:06:53,544
Would it kill her to just pick up?

101
00:06:55,374 --> 00:06:58,344
Of course. She must be very disappointed.

102
00:06:59,544 --> 00:07:02,344
She was shown up by Ko Eun Seol,

103
00:07:02,414 --> 00:07:04,884
whom she thought she could beat blindfolded.

104
00:07:05,284 --> 00:07:07,184
Imagine how heartbroken she must be.

105
00:07:07,254 --> 00:07:09,654
The concept was flawed from the start.

106
00:07:10,024 --> 00:07:11,524
In this day and age,

107
00:07:11,594 --> 00:07:15,294
she should've taken a more realistic and modern approach.

108
00:07:16,624 --> 00:07:19,964
That's always the issue with you.

109
00:07:20,164 --> 00:07:22,064
When our daughter is struggling emotionally,

110
00:07:22,134 --> 00:07:24,274
can't you just sympathize with how she feels?

111
00:07:24,874 --> 00:07:27,144
I'm already a strict and stern father,

112
00:07:27,204 --> 00:07:29,344
but how can a mother be even harsher?

113
00:07:30,004 --> 00:07:31,914
I'm not just her mother.

114
00:07:32,214 --> 00:07:34,414
I'm also Hae Ra's boss.

115
00:07:34,814 --> 00:07:37,754
I'm just trying to remain neutral.

116
00:07:38,214 --> 00:07:40,754
It's because you keep treating Hae Ra like that,

117
00:07:40,824 --> 00:07:42,824
that she keeps drifting away.

118
00:07:43,854 --> 00:07:44,924
Honey.

119
00:07:45,694 --> 00:07:46,864
Unbelievable.

120
00:07:50,024 --> 00:07:51,034
Director Joo.

121
00:07:51,434 --> 00:07:55,304
Am I really that cold as a mother?

122
00:07:58,034 --> 00:08:01,504
It's impossible for a mother to be warm all the time.

123
00:08:02,344 --> 00:08:03,974
I'll keep trying to contact her.

124
00:08:06,514 --> 00:08:09,014
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

125
00:08:14,224 --> 00:08:16,424
Yes, Director Joo. Why are you calling at this hour?

126
00:08:16,654 --> 00:08:20,224
I'm calling because I can't get in touch with Hae Ra.

127
00:08:20,324 --> 00:08:21,664
Are you with her by any chance?

128
00:08:22,524 --> 00:08:25,164
No. I'll try contacting her.

129
00:08:25,634 --> 00:08:28,104
Thank you. That would be great.

130
00:08:28,264 --> 00:08:30,274
If there's trouble, call me right away.

131
00:09:13,714 --> 00:09:16,514
What? Seok Jin, it's you!

132
00:09:19,054 --> 00:09:20,084
Where are you?

133
00:09:43,204 --> 00:09:44,244
Hae Ra.

134
00:09:49,184 --> 00:09:50,514
Seok Jin.

135
00:09:51,554 --> 00:09:53,154
I had a few drinks.

136
00:10:02,424 --> 00:10:03,424
Congratulations.

137
00:10:40,964 --> 00:10:42,004
Hae Ra.

138
00:10:48,804 --> 00:10:50,144
We're here. Wake up.

139
00:10:51,374 --> 00:10:52,374
Hae Ra.

140
00:10:53,074 --> 00:10:54,084
Hae...

141
00:10:56,814 --> 00:10:58,154
Seok Jin.

142
00:11:02,554 --> 00:11:04,854
You're going to marry me, right?

143
00:11:07,764 --> 00:11:09,224
I...

144
00:11:10,964 --> 00:11:14,104
really, really...

145
00:11:15,334 --> 00:11:17,674
like you so, so much.

146
00:11:28,714 --> 00:11:30,754
I like you so much.

147
00:11:32,854 --> 00:11:34,284
I love you.

148
00:11:55,944 --> 00:11:57,044
Chief,

149
00:11:57,144 --> 00:11:59,514
I'd like to treat you to a meal to show my gratitude.

150
00:11:59,714 --> 00:12:01,714
When would be a good time for you?

151
00:12:26,904 --> 00:12:28,674
Gosh, thank you.

152
00:12:29,074 --> 00:12:30,074
It was nothing.

153
00:12:30,144 --> 00:12:32,244
- Well, have a pleasant night. - Right.

154
00:12:33,274 --> 00:12:34,314
Chief Cha.

155
00:12:35,644 --> 00:12:36,644
Yes?

156
00:12:37,454 --> 00:12:40,454
Hae Ra may seem strong on the outside,

157
00:12:40,884 --> 00:12:42,254
but she's actually very fragile.

158
00:12:43,154 --> 00:12:44,954
I need you to take good care of her.

159
00:12:46,094 --> 00:12:47,894
Yes, I will.

160
00:12:49,194 --> 00:12:51,394
All right, you should get going.

161
00:12:51,534 --> 00:12:52,794
Okay, then.

162
00:12:53,564 --> 00:12:54,634
Get home safely.

163
00:13:03,304 --> 00:13:06,174
How's Hae Ra? It looked like she drank a lot.

164
00:13:06,774 --> 00:13:09,214
Yes, I think she had a bit too much.

165
00:13:10,714 --> 00:13:12,654
Of course. She must be very upset.

166
00:13:13,214 --> 00:13:15,624
But what can you do? It's all part of the process.

167
00:13:16,324 --> 00:13:18,493
You have to lose badly every once in a while...

168
00:13:18,494 --> 00:13:20,394
in order to grow from it.

169
00:13:22,394 --> 00:13:24,464
Please take good care of her.

170
00:13:25,194 --> 00:13:26,294
Ma'am.

171
00:13:26,864 --> 00:13:27,864
Yes?

172
00:13:28,964 --> 00:13:29,964
Still,

173
00:13:30,264 --> 00:13:33,234
wouldn't it be better if you took this to her yourself?

174
00:13:34,274 --> 00:13:35,504
At least for tonight,

175
00:13:35,674 --> 00:13:38,114
she'll need her mother's sincere comfort.

176
00:13:38,874 --> 00:13:41,714
Right, of course.

177
00:13:41,914 --> 00:13:43,954
Give it here. I'll take it up to her.

178
00:14:18,484 --> 00:14:22,924
Am I really such a bad mother?

179
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:51,184
Mom...

180
00:15:04,094 --> 00:15:06,094
(Cheongma)

181
00:15:13,404 --> 00:15:18,074
Goodness. Come on in. Eun Seol, what brings you here?

182
00:15:19,374 --> 00:15:22,714
I'm so grateful that you rescued me from the storage room that day.

183
00:15:22,784 --> 00:15:24,784
I felt I hadn't properly thanked you.

184
00:15:27,924 --> 00:15:30,484
Oh, you shouldn't have.

185
00:15:31,194 --> 00:15:32,194
By the way,

186
00:15:32,924 --> 00:15:36,194
how did you know I was there that day?

187
00:15:36,794 --> 00:15:37,794
Oh, that?

188
00:15:38,234 --> 00:15:41,734
You didn't show up, so I went looking for you.

189
00:15:42,064 --> 00:15:43,804
Right, I see.

190
00:15:44,804 --> 00:15:46,833
I don't know what went wrong,

191
00:15:46,834 --> 00:15:48,774
but even the circuit breaker had tripped.

192
00:15:50,044 --> 00:15:51,774
You must've been so scared, Eun Seol.

193
00:15:52,174 --> 00:15:54,744
Yes. But thanks to you,

194
00:15:54,814 --> 00:15:56,744
I was able to finish the competition.

195
00:15:56,944 --> 00:15:57,954
Thank you.

196
00:15:58,354 --> 00:16:01,084
Of course I helped. I told you, didn't I?

197
00:16:01,424 --> 00:16:04,554
You can lean on me when things are tough.

198
00:16:05,594 --> 00:16:09,194
Whatever trouble you're having, you can tell me about it, okay?

199
00:16:10,794 --> 00:16:12,564
Yes, I will.

200
00:16:13,594 --> 00:16:14,734
This is a bit late,

201
00:16:14,864 --> 00:16:17,204
but congratulations on your design being chosen.

202
00:16:18,934 --> 00:16:20,034
Thank you.

203
00:16:20,634 --> 00:16:23,144
- Well then. - Okay. You should go.

204
00:16:28,144 --> 00:16:30,184
She's quite the little fox.

205
00:16:34,154 --> 00:16:35,853
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

206
00:16:35,854 --> 00:16:37,554
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

207
00:16:38,424 --> 00:16:40,224
Trying to win people over...

208
00:16:40,294 --> 00:16:41,894
with such cheap junk?

209
00:16:43,864 --> 00:16:47,504
First, we'll start a new project with the selected mass-market line.

210
00:16:48,204 --> 00:16:50,564
The key feature of Ko Eun Seol's design...

211
00:16:50,734 --> 00:16:53,273
was adding function to the mass-market line.

212
00:16:53,274 --> 00:16:55,774
We need to flesh out the details of that functionality.

213
00:16:57,644 --> 00:16:59,674
By utilizing the magnetic push-and-pull principle...

214
00:16:59,744 --> 00:17:01,414
and designing it around the arch of the foot,

215
00:17:01,514 --> 00:17:03,944
we'll highlight its functionality as a shoe.

216
00:17:04,254 --> 00:17:07,484
We want people to wear our shoes to relieve muscle pain...

217
00:17:07,624 --> 00:17:10,084
and provide stable full-body support simply by walking,

218
00:17:10,184 --> 00:17:11,954
allowing anyone to maintain...

219
00:17:12,024 --> 00:17:14,194
a proper gait comfortably and easily in their everyday lives.

220
00:17:22,804 --> 00:17:24,274
Sorry I'm late.

221
00:17:25,974 --> 00:17:27,234
Let's continue with the meeting.

222
00:17:41,684 --> 00:17:43,154
Congratulations, Ko Eun Seol.

223
00:17:44,524 --> 00:17:47,094
You got luckier than expected, right?

224
00:17:48,364 --> 00:17:51,564
I won with skill, not luck, Ms. Kang.

225
00:17:53,564 --> 00:17:56,034
Fine, let's call it skill.

226
00:17:57,304 --> 00:17:59,234
But do you know what beats skill?

227
00:18:01,844 --> 00:18:03,844
It's power.

228
00:18:07,944 --> 00:18:10,954
Keep grinding from the ground up and build your skills.

229
00:18:11,814 --> 00:18:13,484
I'll be using my power to win.

230
00:18:13,584 --> 00:18:14,784
You and I...

231
00:18:15,754 --> 00:18:16,984
are in different leagues.

232
00:18:19,594 --> 00:18:21,194
Keep up the work, Ms. Ko.

233
00:18:31,274 --> 00:18:34,644
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

234
00:18:40,074 --> 00:18:43,944
I'd like to treat you to a meal to show my gratitude.

235
00:18:44,214 --> 00:18:46,154
When would be a good time for you?

236
00:18:47,154 --> 00:18:51,724
(Ko Eun Seol)

237
00:18:53,494 --> 00:18:56,224
Chief, I'm sending you the file you requested.

238
00:18:56,294 --> 00:18:59,494
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

239
00:18:59,564 --> 00:19:00,664
Thank you.

240
00:19:06,004 --> 00:19:08,674
If you happen to be free tomorrow,

241
00:19:08,744 --> 00:19:10,104
how about we grab a bite to eat?

242
00:19:19,384 --> 00:19:21,254
Did something good happen, Eun Seol?

243
00:19:23,624 --> 00:19:24,624
No.

244
00:19:25,294 --> 00:19:26,454
It's nothing.

245
00:19:51,314 --> 00:19:52,353
(Cha Seok Jin: If you happen to be free tomorrow, )

246
00:19:52,354 --> 00:19:53,354
(how about we grab a bite to eat?)

247
00:19:55,324 --> 00:19:57,654
So they're meeting behind my back?

248
00:20:05,864 --> 00:20:07,334
Eun Seol, here you go.

249
00:20:07,534 --> 00:20:09,204
Right, thank you.

250
00:20:15,644 --> 00:20:18,844
I feel a little awkward in places like this.

251
00:20:20,174 --> 00:20:22,814
Why? Seeing you here, Eun Seol,

252
00:20:23,214 --> 00:20:24,484
makes you look even more stunning.

253
00:20:25,184 --> 00:20:26,954
Are you teasing me?

254
00:20:27,984 --> 00:20:29,254
No, I'm serious.

255
00:20:30,384 --> 00:20:32,324
- Please dig in. - Okay.

256
00:20:39,664 --> 00:20:43,004
It may be a little awkward, but the food is delicious.

257
00:20:57,954 --> 00:21:02,024
Sometimes, this all feels like a dream.

258
00:21:04,084 --> 00:21:06,494
Back when I was in prison,

259
00:21:07,194 --> 00:21:09,524
I could never have imagined something like this.

260
00:21:10,794 --> 00:21:13,194
I had a vengeful determination...

261
00:21:13,534 --> 00:21:15,564
that drove me to uncover the real killer,

262
00:21:16,434 --> 00:21:18,674
but honestly, I had no hope.

263
00:21:20,374 --> 00:21:23,344
Then again, that determination might've gotten me this far.

264
00:21:24,774 --> 00:21:28,184
But lately, I've started to feel a little hope.

265
00:21:30,284 --> 00:21:32,584
That maybe I can be happy...

266
00:21:32,984 --> 00:21:34,924
like other people.

267
00:21:35,954 --> 00:21:38,154
I've been feeling so excited lately...

268
00:21:38,394 --> 00:21:40,554
with those kinds of ordinary expectations.

269
00:21:44,264 --> 00:21:45,764
I would like to share...

270
00:21:46,694 --> 00:21:48,264
that ordinary happiness with you.

271
00:21:50,334 --> 00:21:51,334
What?

272
00:21:59,774 --> 00:22:00,774
Eun Seol.

273
00:22:01,514 --> 00:22:03,314
Who am I to you?

274
00:22:06,814 --> 00:22:08,884
I want to protect...

275
00:22:09,854 --> 00:22:11,094
your ordinary happiness.

276
00:22:12,654 --> 00:22:13,824
Not as your lawyer,

277
00:22:14,794 --> 00:22:16,064
but as your man.

278
00:22:21,504 --> 00:22:22,504
I...

279
00:22:23,234 --> 00:22:26,934
I haven't really thought about you that way.

280
00:22:28,374 --> 00:22:30,104
I'm sorry, Attorney Seo.

281
00:22:38,884 --> 00:22:40,184
Gosh, my bad.

282
00:22:41,384 --> 00:22:42,854
That caught you off guard, didn't it?

283
00:22:43,784 --> 00:22:44,824
I just...

284
00:22:45,154 --> 00:22:47,424
want you to be happy, like you are now.

285
00:22:48,194 --> 00:22:49,494
That's all I meant by it.

286
00:22:50,394 --> 00:22:52,134
Please don't feel pressured.

287
00:22:54,864 --> 00:22:55,864
Okay.

288
00:22:59,134 --> 00:23:00,874
If you're finished, shall we head out?

289
00:23:01,904 --> 00:23:03,674
How about we go get some ice cream?

290
00:23:06,444 --> 00:23:07,444
Sounds great.

291
00:23:21,364 --> 00:23:22,724
What are you doing up?

292
00:23:23,594 --> 00:23:24,694
I couldn't sleep.

293
00:23:25,494 --> 00:23:26,794
Should I make you a snack?

294
00:23:27,634 --> 00:23:29,904
It's okay. I'm just going to have this.

295
00:23:31,134 --> 00:23:33,404
Why? Is something on your mind?

296
00:23:34,374 --> 00:23:36,544
There's someone I've known for a long time,

297
00:23:37,574 --> 00:23:41,314
and I don't want to just be good friends with her anymore.

298
00:23:42,184 --> 00:23:44,514
I want us to become something more,

299
00:23:46,554 --> 00:23:49,084
but I think she feels a bit burdened by it.

300
00:23:50,754 --> 00:23:52,224
What should I do in a situation like this?

301
00:23:53,054 --> 00:23:54,054
You're...

302
00:23:54,924 --> 00:23:56,424
talking about Eun Seol, aren't you?

303
00:23:57,594 --> 00:23:58,834
How did you know?

304
00:23:58,894 --> 00:24:00,393
How could I not know?

305
00:24:00,394 --> 00:24:02,604
It's so obviously about her.

306
00:24:03,664 --> 00:24:06,034
I think Eun Seol still feels pressured.

307
00:24:07,004 --> 00:24:09,274
And I think I was too hasty.

308
00:24:10,804 --> 00:24:11,814
Hyun Jae.

309
00:24:12,914 --> 00:24:15,184
As I've said before,

310
00:24:16,044 --> 00:24:17,644
I have my reservations about Eun Seol.

311
00:24:23,884 --> 00:24:26,054
I know she was wrongfully convicted,

312
00:24:26,154 --> 00:24:28,494
and that she's working harder than anyone right now.

313
00:24:28,564 --> 00:24:31,434
Sure, I think that's very admirable.

314
00:24:32,834 --> 00:24:33,894
But...

315
00:24:34,264 --> 00:24:37,974
do you have to be with someone who has such a dark past?

316
00:24:38,474 --> 00:24:40,704
The thought of her being with my brother...

317
00:24:42,744 --> 00:24:43,904
I don't like it.

318
00:24:45,414 --> 00:24:46,414
Mi Rae, please.

319
00:24:47,614 --> 00:24:49,514
I'm sorry that's all I have to say.

320
00:25:09,364 --> 00:25:11,734
Oh, my. I'm so exhausted.

321
00:25:12,434 --> 00:25:14,404
Oh, dear. Goodness.

322
00:25:17,074 --> 00:25:19,614
Oh, my. Goodness me.

323
00:25:26,014 --> 00:25:28,823
Eun Guk. Look at the state of you.

324
00:25:28,824 --> 00:25:29,824
Oh, this?

325
00:25:30,284 --> 00:25:32,254
Something happened at my part-time job.

326
00:25:32,324 --> 00:25:33,424
What happened?

327
00:25:33,494 --> 00:25:34,964
It's nothing, Grandma.

328
00:25:35,864 --> 00:25:37,994
Oh, my. Eun Guk, wait.

329
00:25:41,664 --> 00:25:43,204
Unbelievable.

330
00:25:43,734 --> 00:25:47,134
What's the point of me living like this?

331
00:25:48,644 --> 00:25:50,274
My only grandson,

332
00:25:50,344 --> 00:25:52,474
whom I doted on and raised so carefully,

333
00:25:52,774 --> 00:25:55,314
ends up getting treated horribly at his part-time job.

334
00:25:56,584 --> 00:25:59,784
Darn. Money is the root of all evil.

335
00:26:02,184 --> 00:26:03,184
That's right.

336
00:26:04,224 --> 00:26:05,724
Yes, the 500,000 dollars!

337
00:26:14,664 --> 00:26:16,334
With that 500,000 dollars,

338
00:26:17,164 --> 00:26:19,534
I'll set my grandson up with something.

339
00:26:19,904 --> 00:26:22,504
I raised a complete stranger for nothing,

340
00:26:22,574 --> 00:26:24,044
so that's the least I deserve.

341
00:26:24,774 --> 00:26:25,774
Hee Jung.

342
00:26:26,144 --> 00:26:28,784
I'm going to find Eun Seol's birth mother...

343
00:26:28,844 --> 00:26:31,084
and use the money to back Eun Guk's business.

344
00:26:31,384 --> 00:26:34,014
So just turn a blind eye and pretend you don't know.

345
00:26:35,124 --> 00:26:37,284
My goodness, where did he hide it?

346
00:26:38,554 --> 00:26:39,554
For goodness' sake.

347
00:26:42,864 --> 00:26:46,094
Here it is. I found it.

348
00:26:48,634 --> 00:26:50,164
- What on earth? - You startled me!

349
00:26:50,804 --> 00:26:51,804
My goodness.

350
00:26:52,974 --> 00:26:55,344
Mom, what are you doing in my room?

351
00:26:55,444 --> 00:26:58,314
What else? For the first time in a while,

352
00:26:59,174 --> 00:27:01,514
I was checking to see if you were sleeping comfortably,

353
00:27:01,914 --> 00:27:03,014
you rascal.

354
00:27:16,464 --> 00:27:17,964
- Have you been waiting long? - Goodness.

355
00:27:19,634 --> 00:27:21,804
But I'm afraid I have bad news.

356
00:27:22,564 --> 00:27:25,074
Even if your daughter-in-law asked you to find this person,

357
00:27:25,274 --> 00:27:27,234
I can't give out private information.

358
00:27:27,534 --> 00:27:28,544
Why not?

359
00:27:31,844 --> 00:27:34,314
My late daughter-in-law, Park Hee Jung,

360
00:27:35,084 --> 00:27:37,914
said she had something important to give to Joo Ae Sook.

361
00:27:38,514 --> 00:27:41,184
I'm telling you, it was her dying wish.

362
00:27:41,254 --> 00:27:42,254
I'm sorry, ma'am.

363
00:27:42,524 --> 00:27:44,283
I have a class to teach.

364
00:27:44,284 --> 00:27:45,294
But...

365
00:27:45,894 --> 00:27:46,894
Honestly.

366
00:27:50,994 --> 00:27:53,534
Private information, my foot.

367
00:27:53,834 --> 00:27:54,864
What a load of bull.

368
00:27:54,964 --> 00:27:56,964
It's only finding one single person,

369
00:27:57,564 --> 00:27:59,734
and you can't even grant a dead person's last wish?

370
00:28:00,374 --> 00:28:03,174
This world is so heartless.

371
00:28:04,004 --> 00:28:05,114
Excuse me, ma'am.

372
00:28:06,074 --> 00:28:08,584
I heard you were Hee Jung's mother-in-law.

373
00:28:09,114 --> 00:28:10,544
Yes, that's right.

374
00:28:11,184 --> 00:28:13,354
I went to high school here...

375
00:28:13,514 --> 00:28:15,224
and was friends with Hee Jung and Ae Sook.

376
00:28:16,054 --> 00:28:18,124
Oh, is that so?

377
00:28:18,554 --> 00:28:20,794
My daughter-in-law's friend was right here.

378
00:28:21,254 --> 00:28:23,894
Ma'am, you're looking for Ae Sook, right?

379
00:28:24,324 --> 00:28:25,334
That's right.

380
00:28:25,994 --> 00:28:28,404
Do you know where Joo Ae Sook is now?

381
00:28:29,204 --> 00:28:32,104
I only know that she's doing well at some large company.

382
00:28:33,374 --> 00:28:35,044
Oh, really?

383
00:28:36,404 --> 00:28:38,474
I heard she changed her name.

384
00:28:39,414 --> 00:28:40,544
To Joo Mi Ran, I believe.

385
00:28:40,944 --> 00:28:42,444
Joo Mi Ran?

386
00:28:43,014 --> 00:28:44,014
Yes.

387
00:28:44,414 --> 00:28:47,054
Anyway, hearing what happened to Hee Jung...

388
00:28:47,554 --> 00:28:49,084
broke my heart.

389
00:28:49,454 --> 00:28:51,454
Right. I see.

390
00:28:52,094 --> 00:28:53,124
Well, thank you.

391
00:28:57,194 --> 00:28:58,194
Hey, there.

392
00:28:59,894 --> 00:29:01,534
So she goes by Joo Mi Ran now?

393
00:29:02,634 --> 00:29:07,274
Joo Mi Ran.

394
00:29:08,144 --> 00:29:09,144
Joo Mi Ran.

395
00:29:09,574 --> 00:29:11,074
You're buying me a meal to thank me?

396
00:29:12,374 --> 00:29:15,344
Yes. Is there anything you want?

397
00:29:16,244 --> 00:29:17,244
Well, I...

398
00:29:18,714 --> 00:29:20,314
Let's have whatever you want.

399
00:29:21,354 --> 00:29:22,354
No way.

400
00:29:23,024 --> 00:29:24,894
This is my treat to thank you,

401
00:29:25,224 --> 00:29:26,824
so you pick the dish.

402
00:29:27,694 --> 00:29:28,694
Okay, then...

403
00:29:30,924 --> 00:29:32,994
Why don't we have that from the old days?

404
00:29:33,834 --> 00:29:34,864
What's that?

405
00:29:40,934 --> 00:29:42,604
Seriously, just tteokbokki?

406
00:29:43,544 --> 00:29:44,774
What do you mean, "just?"

407
00:29:45,244 --> 00:29:46,744
It's been ten years since I last had this.

408
00:29:51,044 --> 00:29:53,114
I couldn't bring myself to eat tteokbokki all this time.

409
00:29:57,254 --> 00:29:59,424
It brought back too many memories, so I couldn't stomach it.

410
00:30:01,354 --> 00:30:03,124
It felt like something was caught in my throat.

411
00:30:12,674 --> 00:30:13,674
It's delicious.

412
00:30:30,654 --> 00:30:31,854
Seok Jin, where are you?

413
00:30:32,494 --> 00:30:35,024
Oh, I'm just meeting with someone.

414
00:30:36,024 --> 00:30:37,024
Really?

415
00:30:42,304 --> 00:30:44,004
What's wrong? What happened?

416
00:30:44,164 --> 00:30:46,504
Seok Jin, I'm hurt.

417
00:30:47,574 --> 00:30:49,704
How did you get hurt? Are you okay?

418
00:30:50,074 --> 00:30:53,044
I'm at the office. Please come right away. Hurry.

419
00:30:53,774 --> 00:30:56,584
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

420
00:31:03,084 --> 00:31:04,084
Was that Hae Ra?

421
00:31:06,354 --> 00:31:07,354
Yes.

422
00:31:09,264 --> 00:31:10,264
You have...

423
00:31:12,134 --> 00:31:13,264
to go, don't you?

424
00:31:19,604 --> 00:31:20,974
Are you going to?

425
00:31:24,944 --> 00:31:26,414
I think Hae Ra got hurt.

426
00:31:27,874 --> 00:31:29,484
I'm sorry. I have to go.

427
00:31:38,694 --> 00:31:40,324
Do you have to be the one to go?

428
00:31:46,164 --> 00:31:47,164
Just...

429
00:31:48,604 --> 00:31:50,064
Can't you just not go?

430
00:32:10,154 --> 00:32:11,154
I'm sorry.

431
00:32:43,024 --> 00:32:45,854
Director Joo, I need you to go to Hae Ra.

432
00:33:15,184 --> 00:33:16,184
Ko Eun Seol.

433
00:33:19,924 --> 00:33:20,924
Seok Jin.

434
00:33:51,484 --> 00:33:55,194
(A Trap Called Desire)

435
00:33:55,264 --> 00:33:56,624
Honestly, Kang Young Hoon.

436
00:33:56,694 --> 00:33:59,694
It's no fun when you give in so easily.

437
00:33:59,894 --> 00:34:02,864
This isn't a position you can get that easily.

438
00:34:03,064 --> 00:34:04,904
You have to find their weakness and exploit it.

439
00:34:05,204 --> 00:34:07,434
Did you have to humiliate me like that in front of everyone?

440
00:34:07,574 --> 00:34:10,104
You're the one making this personal for me.

441
00:34:10,204 --> 00:34:12,514
I'm going to protect her for the rest of my life.

442
00:34:12,614 --> 00:34:15,014
Aren't you engaged to Ms. Kang?

443
00:34:15,214 --> 00:34:17,544
I'd like to have a meal with you, Eun Seol.

444
00:34:17,914 --> 00:34:19,914
Would that make you too uncomfortable?

445
00:34:19,984 --> 00:34:22,124
Ko Eun Seol keeps hitting on Seok Jin,

446
00:34:22,184 --> 00:34:23,554
and he's falling for it.

447
00:34:24,024 --> 00:34:25,824
Is Cha Seok Jin out of his mind?

448
00:34:25,954 --> 00:34:27,724
What is this? Why are you two together?
